## 2. Decisions Log

Decisions agreed so far, which this document builds on:

| # | Topic | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | Releasing a finished node | **Delivery is the ack.** The router collects the report on its poll, stores it in a mailbox for the client, then acks the node. The client's own ack only clears its mailbox and never reaches the node. Safety net: a node-side ack timeout (see §5). |
| D2 | Working branch | If the ticket has `git-branch-id`, that is the working branch. Otherwise the node creates `node/<node-id>/<task-id>`. |
| D3 | Ticket while busy | Rejected immediately with `409 Conflict`. No queueing or caching. |
| D4 | Error reporting | Error reports reuse the `description` field; `status: "error"` marks the failure. |
| D5 | Credentials | Passed by the router per ticket in a `credentials` block. The node holds them in memory for the duration of the task only. |
| D6 | Trust model | LAN-only trust between router and node for the MVP. No transport auth beyond metadata matching. |
| D7 | Worker | Claude Code, driven through the Claude Agent SDK for Python. |
| D8 | Language | Python for the node shell. |

