### 4.1 Components

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **API layer** | FastAPI app exposing the endpoints in §3.1. Pydantic models with kebab-case aliases validate every payload. Contains no business logic; it delegates to the state manager. |
| **Identity validator** | Compares the incoming identity block with the node config. Mismatch → `403`. |
| **State manager** | Owns the single task slot and the state machine (§5). All transitions go through one `asyncio.Lock`. Every transition is persisted to `state.json` before it is acknowledged to the caller. |
| **Registrar** | Registers on startup with backoff. Notes the timestamp of each status poll and re-registers if polls stop (§3.3). |
| **Task runner** | Launches the task as a background `asyncio` task: workspace prep → worker → commit/push → report. Enforces `TASK_TIMEOUT`, catches every exception and turns it into an `error` report. Guarantees the slot always ends in `done` or `error`, never stuck in `busy`. |
| **Workspace manager** | Wraps the `git` CLI. Clones or fetches into a per-task directory, checks out or creates the working branch (D2), computes the diff after the worker runs, commits and pushes. Injects the git token via `GIT_ASKPASS`, so it never lands in `.git/config`. Cleans up the workspace once the task is finished. |
| **Prompt builder** | Turns a ticket into the worker's prompt and system prompt (§6.2). |
| **Worker adapter** | Abstract interface (§6.1). The task runner only talks to this. |
| **ClaudeCodeWorker** | Implementation of the adapter using the Claude Agent SDK. |
| **Report builder** | Combines the worker's summary and the git diff into a spec-compliant report (§7.3). |
| **Credential vault** | Holds the current task's credentials in memory. Exposes them to the workspace manager and the worker as environment variables. Wipes them when the task ends. |
| **Persistence** | Local files under `DATA_DIR`: `state.json` (current slot), `reports/<task-id>.json` (archive), `node-id` (generated once), and rotating logs. |

