## 5. State Machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> idle
    idle --> busy: POST /ticket (valid)
    busy --> done: worker finished, pushed
    busy --> error: any failure / TASK_TIMEOUT
    done --> idle: POST /ack  or  ACK_TIMEOUT
    error --> idle: POST /ack  or  ACK_TIMEOUT
```

| From | Event | To | Side effects |
|---|---|---|---|
| `idle` | valid ticket | `busy` | Persist ticket, start task runner |
| `busy` | task succeeded | `done` | Persist report |
| `busy` | exception, timeout, push failure | `error` | Persist error report |
| `done`/`error` | `POST /ack` | `idle` | Move report to `reports/`, clear slot |
| `done`/`error` | `ACK_TIMEOUT` elapsed (default 30 min) | `idle` | Same as ack; log a warning. Report remains fetchable via `GET /reports/{task-id}` |
| any | node restart while `busy` | `error` | Report: "Node restarted during task; partial work may exist on branch X" |

**Why the timeout matters:** together with D1 it guarantees a node is never held hostage. The normal path is that the router acks right after storing the report. The timeout only covers a router crash or a lost ack.

